                  x:Nat \vdash C[x]\,type \\
                  c \Vdash C[zro] \\
                  x:Nat,h:C[x] \vdash c \Vdash C[suc(x)]
                  \\end{array}}
                  {c \Vdash C[n]}
          %p Much nicer, right? Note that the variable declarations effect both a quantifier and a typing hypothesis. So the special status of typing judgments working like context entries is built into the notation.
          %p The rest of the rules we repeat in HOAS form will be given now in this second-order notation. Many rules will not be repeated because there’s no guesswork in translating them.
